;; Surface-equivalence corpus (JUN-579). Each :pair spells one definition in a
;; sugar surface (.cljk / .edn reader sugar) and in the pure Kotoba core. The
;; gate must compute the Definition CID of both and require equality; each
;; :control changes the meaning and must produce a DIFFERENT CID, so agreement
;; is discriminating.
;;
;; Status honesty: :measured pairs carry the CID recorded by
;; ADR-kotoba-pure-s-expression-core-and-cljk-surface (2026-09-08, amu
;; 473e84ab, `amu definition-cids`). :unmeasured pairs are obligations for the
;; Amu selfhost native gate; no CID is asserted for them here.
;; The ADR printed expressions and CIDs, not whole modules: the `defn` wrappers
;; here are reconstructed, and every :control except the +2 one is authored,
;; not measured. The native gate must confirm both before relying on them.
;; 2026-10-29 (JUN-587): a native aarch64-linux measurement is recorded under
;; :native-measurements-aarch64-linux; the pair entries above keep their original status.
;; x86_64 and macOS have not been measured here.

