  {:id :cap-call-vs-perform
   :status :unmeasured
   :module? true
   :note "ADR records identical wasm32 bytes only; DefCID equality still owed. perform needs the same (:capabilities ..) declaration cap-call does."
   :sugar "(ns d (:export [main]) (:capabilities #{:clock/now}))\n(defn main [] :i64 (perform :clock/now 1))"
   :pure "(ns d (:export [main]) (:capabilities #{:clock/now}))\n(defn main [] :i64 (cap-call :clock/now 1))"
   :control {:source "(ns d (:export [main]) (:capabilities #{:clock/now}))\n(defn main [] :i64 (perform :clock/now 2))" :must :differ}
   :source-evidence ["amu test/nbb/fixtures/pure-product-capability.kotoba:1-6 (cap-call, ns :capabilities)"
                     "amu test/kotoba/compiler/check_cli_test.cljk:70 (perform :clock/now 0 with :capabilities)"
                     "lang/guest-grammar.edn:898 (perform -> cap-call; :state/get and :state/put excluded)"]
   :caveat "Pure spelling here is cap-call, which is the core the ADR names; (perform :state/get|put) is a different route and is NOT used."}
  {:id :try-vs-handle
   :status :unmeasured
   :module? true
   :note "ADR records identical :kir-sha256 and wasm32 bytes; DefCID equality still owed. handle only eliminates :abort; it cannot wrap a capability call (try refuses a body that cannot abort)."
   :sugar "(ns d (:export [main]))\n(defn main [] :i64 (try (if (> 1 0) (throw \"boom\") 5) (catch e 7)))"
   :pure "(ns d (:export [main]))\n(defn main [] :i64 (handle (if (> 1 0) (throw \"boom\") 5) (catch e 7)))"
   :control {:source "(ns d (:export [main]))\n(defn main [] :i64 (handle (if (> 1 0) (throw \"boom\") 5) (catch e 8)))" :must :differ}
   :source-evidence ["lang/conformance/abort/throw_try_one_function.kotoba:7-9 (try/throw/catch)"
                     "amu test/kotoba/compiler/check_cli_test.cljk:73 (handle spelling over throw/catch)"
                     "lang/guest-grammar.edn:900 (handle -> try)"]
   :caveat "handle is refused under :language-profile :pure-product (:kotoba.error/pure-product-forbidden, check_cli_test.cljk:66-76); the gate must use the default profile for this pair."}
